notifications.danger:
The product poses a risk of injuries because:

- the kickstand can be in the down position whilst the motorbike is being ridden and can stick to the ground causing an accident;

- the rear mud guard could break causing the rider to off on to the rear wheel;

- the throttle cable can slightly stick to the frame brackets when turning the handlebar.

The product poses a risk of injuries because:

- back-stops for the  handlebars are missing and the vehicle could turn over during sharp turning;

-   the locking lever for the accelerator can jam resulting in loss of control over the vehicle at full speed;

- the efficiency of the brakes is not sufficient. 


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

