notifications.danger:
This product poses a serious risk of burns, cuts and injuries because : 


- the chain guard is insufficient and therefore there is a danger that the rider will come into contact with the chain; 

- there are sharp edges all over the bike; 

- electrical wiring is exposed to chafing. 


This product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

In certain products, possible seat defects have been discovered during product quality tests. Namely:


- front seat side airbag: the reliability of side airbag deployment on the front seats is insufficient. In the worst case, the side airbag may not offer the expected protection;


- front/rear seat headrest: there is a possibility that the locking performance of the headrest support is insufficient. In some cases this may lead to the headrest coming loose from the locking position during impact. In the worst case it may result in ejection of the headrest from the back seat.

According to the test report, the product does not meet speed sensibility requirements of UNECE instruction Nr. 90: deceleration on 100 km/h and 135 km/h difference can not be more then 15% at deceleration reached by 65 km/h. Laboratory test revealed: 


brake action from 65 km/h deceleration– 5,12 m/s2;


brake action from 100 km/h deceleration– 4,4 m/s2 (14,12% difference);


brake action from 135 km/h deceleration– 3,48 m/s2 (32,14% difference).

