notifications.danger:
This product poses a serious risk of fire, burns and injuries because:


- the fuel pipe is not secured and there is a risk of fuel leakage;

- information regarding stop/switch/tap positions of the fuel system is insufficient; 

- apertures adjacent to rider’s feet are insufficiently guarded to prevent child’s foot touching the engine block and causing burns;

- the chain and the sprocket are insufficiently guarded and exposed parts within 500 mm of seat so there is a risk of catching body parts/clothing in moving chain/sprocket;

- the battery which is located under the seat is not properly secured.


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

This product poses a serious risk of fire, burns and injuries because fuel is being vented out in front of rider which has health, machine control and fire hazard implications. In particular, there is a risk of:



- fire because the fuel pipe is not secured and information regarding stop/switch/tap positions of the fuel system is insufficient;



- burns because apertures adjacent to rider’s feet are insufficiently guarded to prevent child’s foot from touching engine block;



- injuries because the chain and the sprocket are insufficiently guarded and expose parts within 500mm of seat. In addition, there are sharp frontal projections over vehicle’s front lights.



The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

This product poses a serious risk of injuries because of: 


- insufficient mechanical resistance of the materials;

- insufficient stability;

- sharp edges and corners;

- improper  fuel system design;

- excessive noise level;

- incorrect braking system;

- insufficient safety instructions and warnings.


This product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

The product poses a serious risk of injuries because of:


- non-conforming materials used (insufficient mechanical resistance);


- sharp edges and corners;


- missing protective chain guard; 


- non-conforming breaking system;


- non-conforming fuel system design;


- excessive level of noise;


- insufficient safety instructions and warnings.


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

This product poses a serious risk of injuries, fire and cuts because:



- sharp edges are located close to the foot representing a driving hazard;



- moving elements (chain) have no protection to avoid body parts becoming trapped when the product is in operation and to avoid foreign bodies like stones or other objects interfering with its correct operation;



- fingers can get trapped interfering with the normal handling of the drive and control devices which can cause accidents; 



- the petrol pipe is not made of rigid material but of very weak, flexible rubber, which risks cracking in use due to overheating because it is in contact with the exhaust pipe. This results in a risk of explosion because it is located just above the engine.



The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

The product poses a serious risk of injuries because:


- there is insufficient guarding of the engine drive chain and rear-most sprocket;


- the fuel is vented via the filler cap directly in front of the rider which has health, machine control and fire hazard implications;


- the engine stop has no additional action to re-set;
- the handlebar levers are not ball ended;


- the free movement of the steering mechanism is being fouled by mis-aligned body parts;


- sharp edges are also present;


- no user manual is supplied with the machine. 


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

This product poses a risk of injuries because:


- there is insufficient guarding of the engine drive chain and rear-most sprocket;


- the fuel is vented via the filler cap directly in front of the rider which has health, machine control and fire hazard implications;


- the fuel pipe and tank were insecure;


- the engine stop has no additional action to re-set;


- the handlebar levers are not ball ended;


- there was no reserve travel on the off-side brake operating lever (front brake) which means that it cannot achieve full braking efficiency if required;


- the free movement of the steering mechanism was being fouled by mis-aligned body parts. 


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

