notifications.danger:
The product poses a risk of:


- injury because it may suffer fuel loss due to rupture of the high pressure fuel pipe. This is due to the poor quality of the rubber used in the high pressure fuel pipe clamp. As a result, the engine may cut out while the vehicles are being driven on public highways and cause a traffic accident;



- fire because the fuel escaping from the supply line may end up being atomised at high pressure and once in contact with the hottest parts of the engine, such as the exhaust manifolds, could start a fire through ignition of the gaseous mix. This might affect other key systems of the car whose power supply derives from the running engine.

The product is of very poor quality and has many flaws. The poor quality of the construction, bodywork and used parts can lead to premature failure of the bike with a possible injury to the user. In addition, the product suffers from the following deficiencies: 


- fuel tank leaks; 


- no casing around the cylinder which can lead to overheating of the near parts;




- rotating of the back tyre is awkward; 


- exhaust pipe heats up the seat; 


- chains rub against other parts.


The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

The use of this machine is dangerous because:


- the engine drive chain and rear sprocket are insufficiently guarded;

- the fuel is vented via the filler cap directly in front of the rider which has health, machine control and fire hazard implications;

- there are three extremely sharp-pointed plastic parts on the fairing and windshield facing the rider;

- the steering mechanism excessively fouls the engine’s coolant pipe; should this fail whilst the machine was being ridden, very hot water may be sprayed onto the rider; 

-when inverting the machine, an amount of fuel leaks from the vent;

- there is no speed limiting device;

- the handlebar levers are not ball ended and the outer handlebars are misaligned;

- the engine stop has no additional action to reset and the throttle control does not self-close; 

- no user manual is supplied with the machine.

This product poses a risk of injury due to:


- insufficient guarding of chain and sharp edges of chain guard; 


- isolated wire of stop button can contact exhaust pipe;


- there are no means of signalling; 


- it is possible to start machinery without key by unauthorised persons; 


- insufficient user manual, marking and warning information.
The product does not comply with the Machinery Directive.

